# SRG-APP-000925-WSR-000330  -  CAT II
# The web server must compare the internal system clocks on an
# organization-defined frequency with organization-defined authoritative
# time source.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000925-WSR-000330
group:           V-264359
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004923
control_rev5:    SC-45

contribution:    The search head behind Splunk Web compares its clock against each peer's
                 clock at peer registration and during distributed search, and the
                 tolerated difference is the one value the application expresses; the
                 frequency and the authoritative source are not application settings.

governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.

check:           limits.conf [search] addpeer_skew_limit present
check:           limits.conf [search] max_tolerable_skew present

external:        The host operating system's time service, which compares the internal
                 clock with the authoritative time source on its own schedule
external:        The organization-defined comparison frequency and the identity of the
                 authoritative time source
external:        Operating system STIG settings for the time service polling interval

citation:        SRG-APP-000925-WSR-000330 check text; limits.conf.spec:493-502, 529-536
finding:         Splunk expresses no tolerated difference for the clock comparison the
                 search head performs against its peers (limits.conf [search]
                 max_tolerable_skew or addpeer_skew_limit is not available in the assessed
                 configuration), so a divergent clock behind the web interface is neither
                 reported nor refused.
